"=====================\n"
"\n"
"Several AgroMarin customers are related to each other -- by blood, by marriage,\n"
"by *compadrazgo*, or by farming the same land. That is commercially material and\n"
"was recorded nowhere.\n"
"\n"
"**The model.** ``res.partner.relation`` is one row per tie, between two contacts,\n"
"typed by ``res.partner.relation.type``. A type declares which of three algebras it\n"
"follows, because they behave differently and collapsing them loses information:\n"
"\n"
"* *symmetric* -- ``sibling of``, ``cousin of``, ``compadre of``,\n"
"  ``business partner of``, ``grows crop together with``. One row is the whole\n"
"  fact; a mirrored row is rejected, since it would draw two edges and double\n"
"  every degree count.\n"
"* *asymmetric* -- ``parent of`` / ``child of``, ``guarantor of`` /\n"
"  ``guaranteed by``. Stored once, read from either end.\n"
"* *gendered* -- ``father of`` and ``mother of`` are the same type read against a\n"
"  contact's ``gender``, as are ``compadre`` and ``comadre``.\n"
"\n"
"A type also carries a ``category`` (consanguinity, affinity, ritual kinship,\n"
"household, business, agricultural), a civil-law ``degree``, and a ``weight_risk``\n"
"saying how strongly the tie implies a shared economic interest. ``compadre`` is\n"
"the reason ``category`` and ``degree`` are separate axes: ritual kinship carries\n"
"real economic obligation at zero genealogical distance.\n"
"\n"
"**The analysis.** ``res.partner`` gains a breadth-first walk over that graph --\n"
"``_get_related_partners()`` for the related-party group and\n"
"``_get_relation_path()`` for the shortest chain between two contacts, worded from\n"
"each contact's own end (\"Juan -- husband of -> Maria -- compadre of -> Pedro\").\n"
"Both are batched one query per degree, not one per record.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_payment_term
msgid ""
"\n"
"Payment Terms\n"
"=============\n"
"The payment conditions a trade document agrees on: the instalments an amount\n"
"splits into, the date each one falls due, and the discount for paying early.\n"
"Orders show them, invoices schedule their receivables and payables by them,\n"
"payments apply their discounts, and a partner carries one for each direction.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_hr_payroll_sale_commission
msgid ""
"\n"
"Payment of employee commission\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"This application allows you to pay commission in payslips.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Paiement des commissions des employés\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"Cette application permet de payer les commissions dans les fiches de paie.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_hr_appraisal
msgid ""
"\n"
"Periodical Employees appraisal\n"
"==============================\n"
"\n"
"By using this application you can maintain the motivational process by doing "
"periodical appraisals of your employees performance. The regular assessment "
"of human resources can benefit your people as well your organization.\n"
"\n"
"An appraisal plan can be assigned to each employee. These plans define the "
"frequency and the way you manage your periodic personal appraisal.\n"
"\n"
"Key Features\n"
"------------\n"
"* Ability to create employee's appraisal(s).\n"
"* An appraisal can be created by an employee's manager or automatically "
"based on schedule which is defined in the employee form.\n"
"* The appraisal is done according to a plan in which various surveys can be "
"created. Each survey can be answered by a particular level in the employees "
"hierarchy. The final review and appraisal is done by the manager.\n"
"* Manager, colleague, collaborator, and employee himself/herself receives "
"email to perform a periodical appraisal.\n"
"* Every Appraisal Form filled by employees, colleague, collaborator, can be "
"viewed in a PDF form.\n"
"* Meeting Requests are created manually according to employees appraisals.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Évaluation périodique des employés\n"
"==============================\n"
"\n"
"Grâce à cette application, vous pouvez maintenir la motivation en évaluant "
"régulièrement les performances de vos employés. L'évaluation régulière des "
"ressources humaines peut être bénéfique aux employés et à l'entreprise.\n"
"\n"
"Un plan d'évaluation peut être attribué à chaque employé. Ces plans "
"définissent la fréquence et la manière dont vous gérez l'évaluation "
"périodique de votre personnel.\n"
"\n"
"Principales fonctionnalités\n"
"------------\n"
"* Possibilité de créer des évaluations d'employés.\n"
"* Une évaluation peut être créée par un responsable ou être organisée "
"automatiquement selon le calendrier défini dans le formulaire de l'employé.\n"
"* L'évaluation s'effectue selon un plan dans lequel divers sondages peuvent "
"être créés. Chaque sondage peut être complété par un niveau particulier dans "
"la hiérarchie des employés. L'examen et l'évaluation finaux sont effectués "
"par le responsable.\n"
"* Le responsable, le collègue, le collaborateur et l'employé reçoivent "
"chacun un e-mail pour passer une évaluation périodique.\n"
"* Tous les formulaires d'évaluation remplis par les employés, les collègues "
"et les collaborateurs peuvent être affichés au format PDF.\n"
"* Les demandes de réunion sont créées manuellement, en fonction des "
"évaluations des employés.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_voip_speech
msgid ""
"\n"
"Phone - Speech\n"
"==============\n"
"\n"
"``voip`` already records a SIP session and uploads the file when the call ends.\n"
"This files that file as a media segment of the call and queues its\n"
"transcription, so a phone call and a Discuss call answer the same questions\n"
"through the same model: how long is the recording, what was said in it, and can\n"
"it be found by searching for a phrase.\n"
"\n"
"Nothing here knows a vendor, and nothing here indexes anything. The engine is\n"
"whichever one ``speech_ai`` selected, and the transcript is the attachment's\n"
"own index content.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_phone_validation
msgid ""
"\n"
"Phone Numbers Validation\n"
"========================\n"
"\n"
"This module adds the feature of validation and formatting phone numbers\n"
"according to a destination country.\n"
"\n"
"It also adds phone blacklist management through a specific model storing\n"
"blacklisted phone numbers.\n"
"\n"
"It adds mixin.mail.thread.phone mixin that handles sanitation and blacklist of\n"
"records numbers. "
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_it
msgid ""
"\n"
"Piano dei conti italiano di un'impresa generica.\n"
"================================================\n"
"\n"
"Italian accounting chart and localization.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Plan comptable générique de l'entreprise italienne.\n"
"================================================\n"
"\n"
"Plan comptable et localisation pour l'Italie.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_planning_holidays
msgid ""
"\n"
"Planning integration with time off\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Intégration entre Planning et Congés\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_matrix
msgid ""
"\n"
"Please refer to Sale Matrix or Purchase Matrix for the use of this module.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Référez-vous à la Matrice des Ventes ou à la Matrice des Achats pour "
"l'utilisation de ce module.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_pl_hr_payroll
msgid ""
"\n"
"Polish Payroll Rules.\n"
"=========================\n"
"\n"
"    * Employee Details\n"
"    * Employee Contracts\n"
"    * Passport based Contract\n"
"    * Allowances/Deductions\n"
"    * Allow to configure Basic/Gross/Net Salary\n"
"    * Employee Payslip\n"
"    * Integrated with Leaves Management\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Règles de paie polonaises.\n"
"=========================\n"
"\n"
"    * Coordonnées de l'employé\n"
"    * Contrats de l'employé\n"
"    * Contrat basé sur un passeport\n"
"    * Allocations/Déductions\n"
"    * Permet de configurer le salaire de base/brut/net\n"
"    * Fiche de paie de l'employé\n"
"    * Intégré à la gestion des congés\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_test_performance_compare
msgid ""
"\n"
"Portable ORM benchmark for A/B comparison between this fork and a vanilla\n"
"Odoo 19.0 checkout.\n"
"\n"
"Unlike ``test_performance`` (which is fork-only and couples to refactored\n"
"internals such as ``odoo.tests.benchmark``, ``FieldCache``, specialised field\n"
"``__get__``, ``fast_clone`` …), this module is **fully self-contained**:\n"
"\n"
"* depends only on ``base``;\n"
"* defines its own models (no shared data, deterministic state);\n"
"* vendors its own timing + query-count harness (``tests/perfkit.py``) that\n"
"  relies solely on public, version-stable APIs (``cr.sql_log_count`` and\n"
"  ``time.perf_counter_ns``);\n"
"* imports nothing fork-specific, so the whole folder can be dropped, unchanged,\n"
"  into a vanilla 19.0 addons path and produces a comparable result file.\n"
"\n"
"See ``README.md`` for the full A/B runbook.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_auth_portal
msgid ""
"\n"
"Portal Account Security\n"
"=======================\n"
"Exposes the credential management that ``auth_totp`` and ``auth_passkey``\n"
"provide in the backend on the portal's ``/my/security`` page: enabling and\n"
"disabling two-factor authentication, revoking trusted devices, and adding,\n"
"renaming and deleting passkeys.\n"
"\n"
"Merged from the former ``auth_totp_portal`` and ``auth_passkey_portal``. Both\n"
"were ``auto_install`` on ``portal`` plus an always-installed parent, so neither\n"
"could ever exist without the other; they extended the same view and shipped the\n"
"same kind of frontend interaction.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_portal
msgid ""
"\n"
"Portal Framework\n"
"================\n"
"\n"
"Base code for portal-authenticated pages: shared controller class, portal\n"
"mixin, and templates used by business addons to expose records to external\n"
"users (customers, vendors, signers, event attendees, mailing-list subscribers,\n"
"resellers, ...). The display label is \"Customer Portal\" for historical reasons,\n"
"but the technical scope covers any user with portal access rights.\n"
"\n"
"The module deliberately does not depend on website-editing or theming\n"
"capabilities so portal pages can be rendered without the ``website`` module.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_agronomic_docs
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Agronomic Documents\n"
"===========================\n"
"\n"
"Author, manage and print the commercial / agronomic product documents that\n"
"accompany the safety data sheet:\n"
"\n"
"* the **pesticide label** (\"etiqueta\") — the die-cut container label mandated by\n"
"  COFEPRIS / NOM-232 (Mexico) or the EPA-style label (US);\n"
"* the **technical data sheet** (\"ficha técnica\") — the agronomic/marketing sheet;\n"
"* the shared **crop / pest / dose recommendation** table reused by both.\n"
"\n"
"Branding, theme resolution, report language and the draft/publish lifecycle are\n"
"shared with the safety data sheet through ``mixin.product.document``, so this\n"
"module depends on ``product_msds``.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_asset_ledger_maintenance_mrp
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Asset Maintenance / Manufacturing Bridge\n"
"================================================\n"
"\n"
"View glue between ``asset_ledger_maintenance`` and ``mrp``: adds the\n"
"Maintenance submenu (machines & tools, plans, orders) under the Manufacturing\n"
"app's root menu.\n"
"\n"
"Split out of ``asset_ledger_maintenance`` because that module does not\n"
"otherwise depend on ``mrp``, so asset maintenance works without the\n"
"Manufacturing app. Auto-installs where both are present.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_catalog
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Catalog\n"
"===============\n"
"\n"
"The commercial catalog that accompanies the label and the technical data sheet:\n"
"one entry per product, grouped in the sections the printed catalog uses\n"
"(Insecticidas, Fungicidas, Nutrición y Coadyuvante, Bactericidas y Viricidas,\n"
"Herbicidas).\n"
"\n"
"Each entry stores what the printed page shows — the product name artwork, the\n"
"active-ingredient lead, the catalog description, the presentation pictogram and\n"
"the section it belongs to — so adding, archiving or reordering a product is done\n"
"in Odoo instead of editing a design file.\n"
"\n"
"The sanitary-registration flag is derived, not captured: a product counts as\n"
"registered when its label or technical data sheet already carries a registration\n"
"number, as \"no registration required\" when its section does not need one\n"
"(fertilizers, biostimulants and adjuvants), and as \"in process\" while the\n"
"registration is pending. Printing asks for one of those flags and returns only\n"
"the matching products, so each area can share the version it needs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_msds_compliance
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Documents Compliance\n"
"============================\n"
"\n"
"Bridge between the product document authoring apps and the Documents compliance\n"
"tracking, so a published safety data sheet, pesticide label or technical data\n"
"sheet is a tracked document rather than an untracked PDF.\n"
"\n"
"Publishing stamps the generated document with its ``document.type``, the issue\n"
"date and the expiry derived from the type's validity period, which is what puts\n"
"it inside ``documents_compliance``'s expiration, notification and renewal\n"
"machinery. Without this bridge the PDFs are filed correctly but expire silently.\n"
"\n"
"The validity periods are the document types' defaults and are meant to be edited\n"
"per company: an SDS is commonly reviewed every three years, a registered label\n"
"follows its registration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_mrp_plm
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Life Management\n"
"=======================\n"
"\n"
"* Versioning of Bill of Materials and Products\n"
"* Different approval flows possible depending on the type of change order\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Gestion du cycle de vie du produit\n"
"=======================\n"
"\n"
"* Gestion des versions des nomenclatures et des produits\n"
"* Différents flux de validations possibles selon le type d'ordre de "
"modification\n"
"\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_msds
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product Safety Data Sheets\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Author, manage and print GHS-format Safety Data Sheets (SDS / MSDS, Spanish\n"
"HDS) for products. Each sheet holds the 16 standard GHS sections and renders a\n"
"branded PDF.\n"
"\n"
"The header logo, provider block, accent colour and dark tone all come from the\n"
"sheet's manufacturer partner, not from the company's report theme, and the PDF\n"
"embeds its own Archivo typefaces rather than the theme font. A brand is\n"
"configured on the partner's SDS Branding page.\n"
"\n"
"Mexican specifics (toxicological band, regulatory conformity note) are\n"
"optional, data-driven fields, and the shipped regulatory standards decide the\n"
"conformity line, the report language and whether the toxicological band is\n"
"printed at all.\n"
"\n"
"Chemical identity for the composition rows comes from ``product_substance``.\n"
"``product_un_number`` supplies the UN dangerous-goods registry the sheet links\n"
"to, but the transport rows the report prints are the sheet's own overrides;\n"
"nothing derives them from the linked UN entry yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_un_number
msgid ""
"\n"
"Product UN Numbers\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"Generic reference catalogue of UN (ONU) dangerous-goods numbers per the UN\n"
"Model Regulations (the \"Orange Book\"): the four-digit UN number, its proper\n"
"shipping name and transport hazard class.\n"
"\n"
"Independent of any single use case — products reference a UN number for\n"
"transport documentation, and other modules (safety data sheets, delivery,\n"
"stock) can reuse the same catalogue. Extend the shipped data with additional\n"
"UN numbers as needed.\n"
"\n"
"The proper shipping names are shipped in English, as published in the Orange\n"
"Book. The field is translatable, but no Spanish catalogue of names\n"
"(\"denominación oficial de transporte\") is supplied: sourcing the official\n"
"Spanish wording is a regulated data-authoring exercise rather than a\n"
"translation. Until it is done, a Spanish database renders the names in English.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_project_holidays
msgid ""
"\n"
"Project and task integration with holidays\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Intégration des projets et des tâches avec les vacances\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_http_routing
msgid ""
"\n"
"Proposes advanced routing options not available in web or base to keep\n"
"base modules simple.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Propose des options d'acheminement avancées, non disponibles sur le web ou "
"dans la base pour garder\n"
"les modules de base simples.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_website_customer
msgid ""
"\n"
"Publish your customers as business references on your website to attract new "
"potential prospects.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Publiez vos clients comme des références commerciales sur votre site web "
"pour attirer de nouvelles pistes.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_approval_purchase
msgid ""
"\n"
"Purchase Order Approvals\n"
"========================\n"
"\n"
"Approval workflow on ``purchase.order`` through ``mixin.approval``.\n"
"\n"
"Approval triggers, configured per approval category:\n"
"\n"
"* amount inside ``order_amount_min`` / ``order_amount_max``\n"
"* vendors listed in ``order_partner_ids``\n"
"* product categories listed in ``product_categ_ids``\n"
"* vendor debit limit (``check_debit_limit``, ``debit_limit_threshold``)\n"
"* rate limit: more than ``po_rate_limit_count`` orders or\n"
"  ``po_rate_limit_amount`` within ``po_rate_limit_hours``\n"
"\n"
"``po_validation_level`` sets how strict validation is (none / above a manager\n"
"threshold / always). ``order_approval_mode`` only chooses which trigger fields\n"
"the category form shows — every non-empty criterion above constrains matching\n"
"regardless of it. Who approves, and in what order, is the category's steps.\n"
"``po_auto_confirm_on_approval`` confirms the order once approved.\n"
"Settings → Purchase carries the company-level rules.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_quality
msgid ""
"\n"
"Quality Base\n"
"===============\n"
"* Define quality points that will generate quality checks on pickings,\n"
"  manufacturing orders or work orders (quality_mrp)\n"
"* Quality alerts can be created independently or related to quality checks\n"
"* Possibility to add a measure to the quality check with a min/max "
"tolerance\n"
"* Define your stages for the quality alerts\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Base de qualité\n"
"===============\n"
"* Définit des niveaux de qualité qui génèrent des contrôles qualité pour les "
"transferts,\n"
"  les ordres de fabrication ou les ordres de travail (quality_mrp)\n"
"* Les alertes de qualité peuvent être créées de manière indépendante ou en "
"lien avec les contrôles qualité\n"
"* Possibilité d'ajouter au contrôle qualité une mesure avec une tolérance "
"min/max\n"
"* Définit vos étapes pour les alertes de qualité\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_quality_control
msgid ""
"\n"
"Quality Control\n"
"===============\n"
"* Define quality points that will generate quality checks on pickings,\n"
"  manufacturing orders or work orders (quality_mrp)\n"
"* Quality alerts can be created independently or related to quality checks\n"
"* Possibility to add a measure to the quality check with a min/max "
"tolerance\n"
"* Define your stages for the quality alerts\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Contrôle qualité\n"
"===============\n"
"* Définir des niveaux de qualité qui génèrent des contrôles qualité pour les "
"transferts,\n"
"  les ordres de fabrication ou les ordres de travail (quality_mrp)\n"
"* Les alertes de qualité peuvent être créées de manière indépendante ou en "
"lien avec les contrôles de qualité\n"
"* Possibilité d'ajouter au contrôle de qualité une mesure avec une tolérance "
"min/max\n"
"* Définir vos étapes pour les alertes de qualité\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_modbus
msgid ""
"\n"
"Registers the ``modbus`` stream protocol (``modbus://host:port`` for TCP,\n"
"``modbus+rtu:///dev/ttyUSB0?baudrate=9600`` for a serial line, on pymodbus).\n"
"A Modbus device pushes nothing: the stream's ``subscriptions`` name the\n"
"registers, the protocol reads them every ``heartbeat_seconds`` on a thread of\n"
"its own and hands each reading to the worker as a frame; a queued frame writes\n"
"registers or coils.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_mqtt
msgid ""
"\n"
"Registers the ``mqtt`` stream protocol (MQTT 5 over paho, ``mqtt://`` and\n"
"``mqtts://``). A stream of this protocol subscribes to the topics of its\n"
"``subscriptions`` and publishes what its outbox holds; the stream worker that\n"
"leads the database keeps the session open.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_websocket
msgid ""
"\n"
"Registers the ``websocket`` stream protocol (``ws://`` and ``wss://``, on\n"
"websocket-client). A stream of this protocol receives every text or binary\n"
"message as a frame and sends what its outbox holds; the stream worker that\n"
"leads the database keeps the connection open and pings it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_hr_payroll_expense
msgid ""
"\n"
"Reimbursement of expenses in Payslips\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"This application allows you to reimburse expenses in payslips.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Remboursement des dépenses dans les fiches de paie\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"Cette application vous permet de rembourser les dépenses dans les fiches de "
"paie.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_expense
msgid ""
"\n"
"Reinvoice Employee Expense\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Create some products for which you can re-invoice the costs.\n"
"This module allow to reinvoice employee expense, by setting the SO directly "
"on the expense.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Refacturer les dépenses des employés\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Créez quelques produits dont vous pouvez refacturer les coûts.\n"
"Ce module permet de refacturer les dépenses des employés en les intégrant "
"directement la commande client.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_partner_relationship_credit
msgid ""
"\n"
"Related-party credit exposure\n"
"=============================\n"
"\n"
"A credit limit authorized on one contact says nothing about what the rest of that\n"
"contact's family already owes. This bridge aggregates the receivable and the\n"
"overdue balance of everyone reachable through ``partner_relationship``, so the\n"
"question a credit committee actually asks -- *what is this household on the hook\n"
"for* -- has an answer on the partner form.\n"
"\n"
"Each related party is discounted by the strength of the chain reaching it\n"
"(``_get_relation_strength_map``), so a spouse counts for nearly all of their\n"
"balance and a second cousin for little of it. The unweighted totals are shown\n"
"beside it, because the weighting is a judgement and the raw number is not.\n"
"\n"
"It also offers the credit scorecard a ``related_exposure`` dimension -- the share\n"
"of the related parties' receivable that is overdue -- shipped inactive.\n"
"\n"
"**This module warns. It does not enforce.** ``account_credit``'s four-tier\n"
"``credit_status`` and its blocking checks are untouched: whether a family's\n"
"aggregate exposure should refuse an order is a policy decision, and it is not\n"
"made here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_hr
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote - HR Integration\n"
"=======================\n"
"\n"
"Assigns remote devices to employees: ``hr.employee`` and ``device.device``\n"
"carry each other, and the employee form links to the assigned devices and to\n"
"their GPS tracking history.\n"
"\n"
"The device link itself is protocol-agnostic -- an access terminal or a company\n"
"phone is assigned to a person the same way a tracker is. Only the tracking\n"
"history is GPS, which is why ``device_gps`` is still a dependency.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote - IoT Device Management\n"
"==============================\n"
"\n"
"Device management for IoT endpoints, independent of the Odoo IoT Box.\n"
"\n"
"Models\n"
"------\n"
"* ``device.device`` / ``device.kind`` -- the device registry\n"
"* ``device.profile`` -- connection settings, one protocol per config. This\n"
"  module ships HTTP/REST and HTTPS/REST; ``device_mqtt``, ``device_modbus``\n"
"  and ``device_websocket`` add theirs through ``selection_add``\n"
"* ``device.data.log`` / ``mixin.device.data.log`` -- time-series payload storage\n"
"\n"
"Routes\n"
"------\n"
"* ``POST /remote/device/<identifier>/data`` -- device pushes a payload\n"
"* ``POST /remote/device/<identifier>/status`` -- device pushes its status\n"
"\n"
"Devices push to Odoo or Odoo polls them. Bearer token authentication,\n"
"company-scoped records, commands and configuration sent back to the device,\n"
"events and alerts through ``mail``.\n"
"\n"
"Transports\n"
"----------\n"
"A protocol contributes one ``comm_protocol`` value and one method per verb in\n"
"``TRANSPORT_VERBS`` -- ``<protocol>_connect``, ``<protocol>_disconnect``,\n"
"``<protocol>_read_data`` -- plus the ``_protocol_*`` hooks it needs. Nothing\n"
"else in ``device.device`` knows the protocol exists, so a transport that costs a\n"
"dependency lives in its own module: ``device_mqtt``, ``device_modbus``,\n"
"``device_websocket``.\n"
"\n"
"Only HTTP and HTTPS are here, and they cost nothing ``requests`` does not\n"
"already cost. This module needs no third-party client and declares no\n"
"``external_dependencies``, so a site that polls REST sensors installs neither an\n"
"MQTT client nor a PLC library.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_mqtt
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote - MQTT\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Adds the ``mqtt`` value to ``device.device``'s ``comm_protocol`` and the MQTT\n"
"v5.0 connection settings on ``device.profile``.\n"
"\n"
"An MQTT device's connection is an ``integration.stream``: the stream worker\n"
"that leads the database dials the broker (``integration_mqtt``), keeps the\n"
"session open, redials it under the stream's backoff and hands every message to\n"
"the device as a data point. ``mqtt_connect`` and ``mqtt_disconnect`` start and\n"
"stop that stream; nothing here dials from an HTTP worker or a cron.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_modbus
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote - Modbus\n"
"===============\n"
"\n"
"Adds the ``modbus_tcp`` and ``modbus_rtu`` values to ``device.device``'s\n"
"``comm_protocol``.\n"
"\n"
"A Modbus device's link is an ``integration.stream``: the stream worker that\n"
"leads the database holds it (``integration_modbus``), reads the device's\n"
"registers every ``modbus_poll_seconds`` and stores each reading as a data\n"
"point; a write is a frame on the stream's outbox. The device's connection\n"
"state follows the row, and nothing here opens a socket from an HTTP worker or\n"
"a cron.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_websocket
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote - WebSocket\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"Adds the ``websocket`` value to ``device.device``'s ``comm_protocol``.\n"
"\n"
"A WebSocket device's connection is an ``integration.stream``: the stream\n"
"worker that leads the database opens it (``integration_websocket``), pings it\n"
"on the profile's interval, redials it under the stream's backoff and hands\n"
"every message to the device as a data point. ``websocket_connect`` and\n"
"``websocket_disconnect`` start and stop that stream; the connection costs a\n"
"thread in the stream worker and nowhere else.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_dav_sync
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote DAV Sync - CalDAV/CardDAV Server\n"
"=======================================\n"
"\n"
"CalDAV/CardDAV server for synchronizing contacts and calendars with mobile\n"
"devices.\n"
"\n"
"* ``dav.addressbook``, ``dav.calendar``, ``dav.sync.state``,\n"
"  ``dav.conflict.resolution``, ``dav.performance``\n"
"* ``device.device`` extended with DAV fields, used for client authentication\n"
"* ``res.partner`` and ``calendar.event`` extended with vCard / iCalendar\n"
"  serialization\n"
"* two-way sync with conflict resolution, incremental through ETag/CTag; no\n"
"  time-series log, the sync state is mutable\n"
"* service discovery through ``.well-known`` URLs\n"
"\n"
"Protocols: RFC 4918 (WebDAV), RFC 6352 (CardDAV), RFC 4791 (CalDAV), RFC 6764\n"
"(discovery), RFC 6350 (vCard 4.0), RFC 5545 (iCalendar). Tested with DAVx5 on\n"
"Android, native iOS Calendar/Contacts, Thunderbird and Evolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_mobile
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote Mobile - Company Phone as IoT Device\n"
"===========================================\n"
"\n"
"Treats a company-owned Android phone as a first-class ``device.device``, on the\n"
"same footing as a GPS tracker, a smart lock or a camera. It is the phone's home\n"
"module and grows one capability per project phase.\n"
"\n"
"A companion app on the phone pushes to three Bearer-authenticated endpoints, each\n"
"accepting a single record, a list, or a list under a key, so a phone that has been\n"
"out of coverage flushes its whole offline queue in one request:\n"
"* **Location** -- ``/remote/mobile/<identifier>/location``. Each GPS fix is stored\n"
"  as a ``device.data.log.gps`` point, so a phone and a vehicle tracker share the\n"
"  very same fleet map, geofencing and trail tooling (``device_gps`` /\n"
"  ``device_gps_geoengine``).\n"
"* **Call logs** -- ``/remote/mobile/<identifier>/calllog``. Each entry becomes a\n"
"  ``device.call.log``, matched to a ``res.partner`` on the last ten digits of the\n"
"  number, so calls surface on the customer record.\n"
"* **Call recordings** -- ``/remote/mobile/<identifier>/recording``. Audio is stored\n"
"  as an attachment on ``device.call.recording`` and matched to its call log by\n"
"  number and time; unmatched uploads are kept as orphans and reconciled by cron,\n"
"  because the two streams can arrive out of order.\n"
"\n"
"Recording capture depends on the handset's OEM dialer writing files to disk -- no\n"
"Android app can record calls itself since Android 10.\n"
"\n"
"The batch routes answer with ``accepted``, ``duplicates`` and ``skipped``, and a\n"
"batch the device had already sent is a delivery rather than a refusal. See\n"
"``README.rst`` for the response contract the companion app depends on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_mobile_speech
msgid ""
"\n"
"Remote Mobile - Speech\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"A company phone's call log is a media timeline, like a VoIP or a Discuss call. A\n"
"recording that finds its place on a timeline -- by default the call-log entry it\n"
"was matched to -- hands its audio over: the attachment moves to that timeline as\n"
"its next segment and ``speech`` transcribes it. ``_timeline_owner`` says where a\n"
"recording belongs and ``_transcription_eta`` when to transcribe it;\n"
"``conversation_mobile`` answers both for company phones that feed\n"
"conversations. A recording that never matches keeps its audio.\n"
msgstr ""

