#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_asset_fuel_charge
msgid ""
"# Fuel Charge for Use Outside the Schedule (GPS)\n"
"\n"
"Charges each vehicle operator the fuel used **after their scheduled leaving\n"
"time**, or on days without a shift, using GPS telemetry (`device_gps`), the\n"
"employee's work calendar (`resource.calendar`) and the vehicle's own pump\n"
"price (`resource.asset.log` fuel entries). Working hours are never charged.\n"
"Driving before the scheduled entry time is shown for information and charged\n"
"only when the wizard asks for it.\n"
"\n"
"## Flow\n"
"\n"
"1. **Assets → Fuel → Fuel Charge Report** (the Assets app; this fork does not\n"
"   use Odoo's `fleet` module, and its own Fleet app is on its way out). Pick a period (the last complete week by default, up to a year; the cap is\n"
"   the `max_period_days` parameter) and the\n"
"   operators; *Export to Excel* downloads the period as a workbook the fleet\n"
"   reworks by hand (see below), *Preview* / *Print PDF* render the report,\n"
"   *Generate Charges* stores one `product.asset.fuel.charge` per operator,\n"
"   vehicle and week with fuel outside the schedule.\n"
"2. **Fuel Charges** (same menu): draft → *Send to Operator* (the operator\n"
"   checks for discrepancies; *Dispute* records the objection, *Reset to Draft*\n"
"   and regenerate settles it) → *Confirm* → collected. *Print Statement* on any\n"
"   selection renders one page per operator with the daily rows, totals,\n"
"   objections and signature lines: the sheet the operator signs off and the\n"
"   accountant applies. With\n"
"   `product_asset_fuel_charge_payroll` installed, a confirmed charge is picked\n"
"   up by the operator's draft payslip of the period (\"In Payroll\") and closed\n"
"   when that payslip is validated; without it, *Mark as Charged* closes it by\n"
"   hand. Closing books a **fuel recovery** log on the vehicle\n"
"   (`resource.asset.log`, log type `fuel_recovery`, product \"Fuel charged to\n"
"   the operator\", with the operator, litres and amount), so the vehicle's net\n"
"   fuel cost is what the company paid at the pump minus what the operator\n"
"   paid back. Re-running the wizard refreshes draft days and leaves confirmed\n"
"   ones alone.\n"
"\n"
"The counterpart of a charge is therefore the vehicle's own fuel purchases\n"
"(the fuel-card credit logs): the charge recovers part of that cost, it never\n"
"adds a cost.\n"
"\n"
"## The workbook\n"
"\n"
"*Export to Excel* is the deliverable the fleet actually edits before\n"
"payroll, so its arithmetic stays live instead of being pasted values:\n"
"\n"
"- **Datos** — one row per operator, vehicle and window (in hours / out of\n"
"  hours), with start, end, hours, distance, odometers, price per litre, km/L,\n"
"  week number, the charged flag and the rule an operator is on. *Litres* is\n"
"  `=km / km/L` and *Discount* is `=litres × price × charged`, so a corrected\n"
"  kilometre or price flows to every total. Autofilter on every column, panes\n"
"  frozen on the operator and vehicle. The totals row is `SUMIFS` over the\n"
"  whole column, so rows added by hand count too.\n"
"- **Dinámica** — discount by operator (or by vehicle, with *Group by*\n"
"  Vehicle) and numbered week, as `SUMIFS` over Datos, plus hours, distance\n"
"  and litres out of hours; ordered by what is owed, the PDF's order.\n"
"- **Recargas con tarjeta** — with `product_asset_fuel_charge_wallet`, every\n"
"  fuel-card refuel of the period.\n"
"\n"
"Cached values are written next to each formula, so a viewer that does not\n"
"recalculate (a phone, a preview) still shows the report's own figures.\n"
"\n"
"The **Fuel Charges** list is editable in place for the adjustment, its\n"
"reason and the notes, and groups by operator, vehicle, week, month, fuel or\n"
"status; once a charge is in payroll, charged or cancelled, the adjustment is\n"
"locked so the payslip and the charge keep the same figure.\n"
"\n"
"## Rule\n"
"\n"
"1. The operator of a vehicle on a day is the holder of its\n"
"   `resource.assignment` with `custody_role = 'operator'`, read as an\n"
"   employee through `asset_ledger_hr`.\n"
"2. Every GPS position is converted to the operator's time zone and compared\n"
"   with the earliest `hour_from` and the latest `hour_to` of the calendar\n"
"   attendance for that weekday, widened by the optional tolerance. Positions\n"
"   after the leaving time, or on a day with no attendance line, are charged;\n"
"   positions before the entry are reported, and charged only with\n"
"   *Charge before entry*.\n"
"3. Litres are *measured* (sum of `fuel_consumed` on those positions) when the\n"
"   vehicle reports a fuel level and the period's consumption stays under the\n"
"   plausibility limit in L/100 km; otherwise *estimated* (or *unreliable*,\n"
"   when a sensor exists but fails the limit) as km driven outside the\n"
"   schedule divided by the reference km/L.\n"
"4. Price per litre: the average of the vehicle's fuel logs (amount ÷ litres)\n"
"   over the 90 days before the period ends; a vehicle without refuels takes\n"
"   the wizard's default for its `resource.asset.vehicle.fuel_type`\n"
"   (gasoline / diesel), related to the vehicle product's `fuel_type` in\n"
"   `fleet`.\n"
"5. Amount = litres × price.\n"
"\n"
"Defaults for the two prices, reference efficiency, tolerance and plausibility\n"
"limit are `ir.config_parameter` keys under `product_asset_fuel_charge.*`.\n"
"\n"
"## Known limits\n"
"\n"
"- Distance is the sum of `real_odometer` steps between consecutive positions,\n"
"  dropping any step of 100 km or more (device resets). A step is attributed to\n"
"  the bucket of the position that closes it, so the segment straddling the\n"
"  leaving time counts as after leaving.\n"
"- `odometer_valid` is deliberately ignored: devices report whole kilometres,\n"
"  so the processor's implied-speed check flags the reading that carries each\n"
"  +1 km step as invalid and keeps the flat ones. Filtering on the flag yields\n"
"  zero distance for every vehicle. That is a `device_gps` defect to fix at the\n"
"  source.\n"
"- The calendar's weekly rotation (`week_type`) is ignored: the earliest entry\n"
"  and latest leaving time across both weeks are used.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_asset_fuel_charge_payroll
msgid ""
"# Fuel Charge: Payroll Deduction\n"
"\n"
"Bridge between `product_asset_fuel_charge` and Mexican payroll. Auto-installs\n"
"when both are present.\n"
"\n"
"- A **draft payslip** picks up every *confirmed* fuel charge of its employee\n"
"  dated inside its period that no other payslip holds, marks them \"In\n"
"  Payroll\", and keeps one input line of the SAT deduction type whose code is\n"
"  `product_asset_fuel_charge_payroll.input_type_code` (default `d_004`, \"Otros -\n"
"  deducción\") equal to their total. The line is named \"Fuel outside schedule:\n"
"  N L, D day(s)\"; other lines of the same type, typed by hand, are untouched.\n"
"- Changing the payslip's employee or dates moves charges in and out.\n"
"- **Validating** the payslip closes its charges (\"Charged\") and books the\n"
"  fuel-recovery log on each vehicle. **Cancelling** it releases them back to\n"
"  \"Confirmed\" so the next payslip takes them.\n"
"- The payslip form shows a \"Fuel Charges\" smart button with the amount.\n"
"\n"
"The salary structure must consume the input: the Mexican structures do, via\n"
"the rule `result = inputs['d_004'].amount * -1`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_product_asset_fuel_charge_wallet
msgid ""
"# Fuel Charge: Wallet Card Refuels\n"
"\n"
"Bridge between `product_asset_fuel_charge` and the electronic wallets\n"
"(`asset_wallet`, so the fuel card of a vehicle is a `wallet.card` held\n"
"by its asset). Auto-installs when both are present.\n"
"\n"
"- The price per litre of a vehicle is the average of its fuel-card\n"
"  `wallet.transaction` rows (amount / litres) over the 90 days before the\n"
"  period ends, source \"wallet\"; the asset fuel logs remain the fallback, then\n"
"  the fuel-type default.\n"
"- The period report shows, per vehicle and in the fleet total, the litres and\n"
"  amount loaded on the fuel card inside the period, next to what the vehicle\n"
"  burned.\n"
"\n"
"Transactions reach the wallet from the issuer's scraper (`web_scraper_efectivale`\n"
"books the Efectinet export) or a manual import.\n"
msgstr ""

